'''Haitan''' or sometimes called '''Sanrobone''' is the smallest continent on [[Adonia|Adonia's]] and the seventh most populous.


==Etymology==
The name Haitan came from [[Zong language]] word 海壇 which means Sea Altar or Sea Terrance. The name is generally used to describe the landform west of [[Abyala]] by Zong explorers and later used widely to recognize it in general. However there is also the theory of Haitan came from the word '''Haitham''', which means Young Hawk in [[w:Arabic language|Parani language]] which is parallel to the naming of Abyala. 

Meanwhile, the name Sanrobone comes from the [[w:Buginese language|Ugise language]]: ''Sanro'' means sage or wise person and ''bone'' means sand or land, which can be translated into "land of sage", The term is given [[Pre-colonial Abyala|exploration]] of western sandbank of Lumpobone ([[Abyala]]) by [[Sultanate of Maros]] on 15th century.

The usage of both Haitan and Sanrobone are used interchangeably to describe the continent, however internationally the name Haitan used more while Sanrobone is used mostly by [[Sanrobonia]] and some extent [[Balausia]] and [[Pangkajene]].

